url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109390","id":3164138484,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc68mOv0","user":{"login":"nepo-dev","id":8767085,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3NjcwODU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8767085?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nepo-dev","html_url":"https://github.com/nepo-dev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nepo-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nepo-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nepo-dev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nepo-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nepo-dev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nepo-dev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nepo-dev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nepo-dev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nepo-dev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-07T13:09:31Z","updated_at":"2025-08-07T13:09:31Z","body":"Hi! You're completely right! I was too quick to hit the \"new issue\" button, since I found a couple doc pages that mention you shouldn't do that after that [[1](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/physics/kinematic_character_2d.html#scene-setup), [2](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_collisionshape3d.html#description)]\n\nStill, I find it strange that the collision breaks specifically if you scale a CharacterBody3D and do nothing to it. If you move it or rotate it, it's fixed. If you try with a StaticBody3D instead, it works. I also tried scaling the CollisionShape3D (it works) and the Shape object (ofc this works too). I suppose this is why it's recommended to edit the shape directly 😅 \n\nI'll leave a video and the project files here in case someone wants to play around with this, but I'll close the issue. Thank you!\n